As shown in Figures fig:menu-dynamics--fig:rl-estimators and Table tab:robust-family, Harness-G trains stably and transfers across backbones and RL algorithms.

#### Stable Optimization across Datasets.

Across all six 3B runs, training-batch F1 rises without persistent late-stage collapse, with bounded gradient norms (Figure fig:menu-dynamics). On 2Wiki, the 3B run leads Search-R1, IGPO, and Graph-R1 throughout training and finishes with the highest F1 (Figure fig:method-f1). Appendix app:robust reports numeric ranges and per-dataset traces.

#### Backbones and RL Algorithms.

On HotpotQA under a matched budget, Qwen2.5-3B, Qwen3.5-4B, and Llama-3.2-3B all reach competitive F1 under the same GRPO recipe (Table tab:robust-family), so the method is not specific to one backbone family. Fixing Qwen2.5-3B and the 120-step budget, GRPO, PPO, REINFORCE++, and DAPO [schulman2017ppo, hu2025reinforcepp, shao2024deepseekmath, yu2025dapo] all rise stably, with GRPO slightly ahead of DAPO (Figure fig:rl-estimators; Appendix app:robust). We use GRPO elsewhere unless stated otherwise.

